# Test First

For behavioral changes, write or update focused tests before changing production code.

Guidance verified: 2026-07.

## Requirements

- Add or update tests first for changes that alter runtime behavior, security controls, data access, routing, persistence, or public API responses.
- Keep documentation-only edits, local-only planning, and generated artifact refreshes scoped and reviewable.
- Do not weaken existing tests to make implementation easier.
- If a package path, import path, environment variable, database identifier, or deployment name changes, add verification for the old and new behavior as appropriate.
- Run the narrowest relevant tests while iterating, then the broader required suite before commit.

## Exceptions

Test-first may be skipped only for:

- Documentation-only edits.
- Local-only planning artifacts.
- Mechanical generated artifacts after their source-of-truth file changed.
- Fixes under 5 lines when the maintainer explicitly approves skipping.

When in doubt, write the test.
